-- Interpretation Act 1984 (WA), compilation 07-k0-00 (the 0H copy at
-- _jurisdiction/sources/interpretation-act-1984.mrdoc_49111.txt): ss 16(2), 37(1)(b) and the s 5
-- definitions of "repeal" and "amend", and s 74, which decide forks FK-04, FK-21 and FK-26 of this subject.
-- A subject-level boundary module, beside the byte-identical copy of the jurisdiction library module
-- wa-interpretation-act-1984.l4 (ss 61, 62, 71, 72), which is not edited. These provisions are not in the
-- reference register: they are one step deeper than depth 1, taken because a fork turns on them (see
-- ENCODING-NOTES.md). LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`

§ `Section 16 -- Reference to written law is to written law as amended`

-- s 16(2): "A reference in a written law to a provision of a written law shall be construed as a reference
-- to such provision as it may from time to time be amended." So "this section" in s 30(1)(b), and "this
-- section" in s 31A(2)(b)(ii), reach the section in each version it has had (FK-04, reading taken A).
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 16(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(2) -- a reference to section 30 reaches` p IF
        (p EQUALS `section 30`)
    OR  (p EQUALS `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024`)

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 16(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(2) -- a reference to section 31A reaches` p IF
        (p EQUALS `section 31A`)
    OR  (p EQUALS `section 31A as in force before 29 July 2024`)

§ `Section 5 -- "amend" and "repeal"; section 37 -- General savings on repeal`

-- s 5: "amend means replace, substitute, in whole or in part, add to or vary"; "repeal includes rescind,
-- revoke, cancel, or delete". The Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2024 s 25(b) deleted "6 months" in
-- s 30(1)(b) and inserted "12 months": the deletion is a repeal of those words.
DECLARE `Amending instruction` IS ONE OF
    `delete words`
    `delete words and insert other words`
    `insert words`

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 5 "repeal"
GIVEN i IS AN `Amending instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 -- the instruction repeals the words it deletes` i IF
        (i EQUALS `delete words`)
    OR  (i EQUALS `delete words and insert other words`)

-- s 37(1)(b): "Where a written law repeals an enactment, the repeal does not, unless the contrary
-- intention appears -- ... (b) affect the previous operation of the enactment repealed or anything duly
-- done or suffered under that enactment". Whether a contrary intention appears is the question FK-21 asks
-- of s 100(4).
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 37(1)(b)
GIVEN `duly done under the enactment before the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears`                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37(1)(b) -- the repeal leaves the thing unaffected, it having been duly done before:` `duly done under the enactment before the repeal` `, a contrary intention appearing:` `the contrary intention appears` IF
        `duly done under the enactment before the repeal`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 74 -- Prescribed forms, certain deviations do not invalidate`

-- s 74: "Where a form is prescribed or specified under a written law, deviations therefrom not materially
-- affecting the substance nor likely to mislead shall not invalidate the form used." Read by FK-26 (reading
-- taken A) where a rent notice is in the form approved by the Minister and the section requires the form
-- approved under s 88C, or the reverse. Whether a deviation is material or misleading is a fact.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 74
GIVEN `the deviations do not materially affect the substance and are not likely to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 74 -- the form used is not invalidated, its deviations being immaterial and not misleading:` `the deviations do not materially affect the substance and are not likely to mislead` IF
    `the deviations do not materially affect the substance and are not likely to mislead`
